# Copy this file to .env, in this folder, and paste your keys in THAT copy.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ⚠️ Keep this file's values EMPTY. It is the template, and unlike .env it is
# NOT gitignored — a key pasted here is a key that gets committed, pushed and
# submitted with the project. If you have already done it, clear the value and
# rotate the key rather than assuming nobody noticed.
#
# Both of these are SECRETS, unlike the app's Clerk publishable key. They are
# billable and they must never reach the phone: anything named EXPO_PUBLIC_* is
# inlined into the app bundle at build time and can be read out of a shipped
# app. That is exactly why these calls live in this service instead of in the
# app.
#
# service/.env is gitignored. Do not commit it, and do not paste a key into
# chat, a screenshot, or the project README.
#
# Each key powers one endpoint and nothing else. Missing either one returns 503
# from that endpoint — a setup problem, not a failure — and everything else
# keeps working.

# POST /analyse — reading a garment out of a photograph.
# Free from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# POST /try-on — FASHN Virtual Try-On v1.6, hosted on fal (see tryon.py).
# From https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys
FAL_KEY=

# GET/PUT /wardrobe — the per-account wardrobe store (see db.py). Missing
# this returns 503 from /wardrobe and /wardrobe/images only; the other four
# endpoints do not touch it and keep working either way.
#
# From your Supabase project: Settings → Database → Connection string →
# "Connection pooling" tab, Transaction mode. Paste it here, then change its
# postgresql:// prefix to postgresql+psycopg:// so SQLAlchemy picks psycopg.
DATABASE_URL=

# Verifying who is calling GET/PUT /wardrobe, without needing Clerk's secret
# key — see auth.py. From your Clerk dashboard: API Keys → Advanced → JWKS
# URL (or build it from your Frontend API domain:
# https://<your-frontend-api>/.well-known/jwks.json).
CLERK_JWKS_URL=

# The same Frontend API domain alone, without the /.well-known/... suffix —
# must match the "iss" claim Clerk puts in every session token, e.g.
# https://your-app-name.clerk.accounts.dev
CLERK_ISSUER=

# POST /wardrobe/images — uploading garment photos to Supabase Storage so
# they follow the wardrobe to another device (see storage.py). Create a
# public bucket named "wardrobe-photos" first (Storage → New bucket).
#
# Both from your Supabase project's Settings → API. The second is the
# SERVICE ROLE key, not the anon/public one — it bypasses row-level security
# entirely, which is exactly why it lives here and never in the app bundle.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=